# Code Review Checklist

## Purpose

Self-review gate before presenting changes as complete.

## Correctness

- [ ] Solves the stated problem only (no scope creep)
- [ ] Edge cases handled (empty, null, unauthorized, timeout)
- [ ] Error paths return consistent shapes

## Architecture

- [ ] Code lives in the correct layer (presentation / application / domain / infra)
- [ ] No circular or cross-feature deep imports
- [ ] Dependencies injected, not hard-coded globals

## Security

- [ ] Inputs validated at boundary
- [ ] No secrets in code, logs, or commits
- [ ] AuthZ checked server-side for protected actions

## Quality

- [ ] Types explicit on public boundaries
- [ ] No debug logging left behind
- [ ] Tests added or updated for behavior change

## Docs

- [ ] README / API docs updated if behavior changed
- [ ] Breaking changes called out in response

## AI-Specific

- [ ] No redundant comments stating the obvious
- [ ] No wholesale reformat of unrelated files
- [ ] Assumptions labeled for human review